<h2><b>Add Collaborators</b></h2>

<h4><b>Add collaborators affiliated with U of T</b></h4>

<ol>
	<li>Confirm that the collaborator you are trying to add has created an account on U of T Dataverse (refer too Create an Account for more information).</li>
	<li>Go to your dataverse collection or dataset</li>
	<li>On the right side, click Edit (or Edit Dataset)</li>
	<li>Select Permissions (for datasets, select Permissions &rarr; Dataset)</li>
	<li>Click the Users/Groups heading</li>
	<li>Click Assign Roles to Users/Groups</li>
	<li>In the User/Group field, start typing the name of the user you wish to add and they will appear in the dropdown menu</li>
	<li>Select the user you wish to add</li>
	<li>Select the role you want to assign to the user</li>
	<li>Click Save Changes</li>
</ol>

<br>
<hr>

<h4><b>Add collaborators outside of U of T</b></h4>

<p>Only users who are affiliated with U of T and have a UTORid can create a dataverse collection or dataset in U of T Dataverse. However, once you have created a dataverse collection or dataset, you can add external collaborators. The person you would like to add must first sign up for an account with Borealis. After the external collaborator has registered their external collaborator account, the dataverse collection or dataset administrator can add them as a collaborator.</p>

<h5><b>To register as an external collaborator:</b></h5>

<ol>
	<li>Go to <a href="https://borealisdata.ca/dataverse/dv">U of T Dataverse</a></li>
	<li>Click Log In in the top right corner of the navigation bar</li>
	<li>Under Underneath Institution not listed? click Sign up</li>
	<li>Register with your preferred email</li>
</ol>

